WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.134 --> 00:00:17.310
The girls who didn't like Sara began to secretly call her "Princess Sara."

2
00:00:17.311 --> 00:00:20.269
They used the name to mock her.

3
00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:24.761
Those who did like Sara also thought it was the perfect name for her.

4
00:00:24.762 --> 00:00:28.777
They used the name kindly, but never in front of her.

5
00:00:28.778 --> 00:00:32.831
Even Miss Minchin began to think of Sara as royalty.

6
00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:37.786
The headmistress told some parents that a real princess was attending the school.

7
00:00:37.787 --> 00:00:42.525
She thought it made the school sound like a sort of royal boarding school!

8
00:00:42.526 --> 00:00:47.659
To Becky, Sara truly did seem like a real princess.

9
00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:55.282
Every day the servant girl finished her chores quickly so that she could visit her friend.

10
00:00:55.283 --> 00:01:00.074
Sara told Becky long and wonderful stories and gave her food.

11
00:01:00.075 --> 00:01:04.757
"I have to be careful about eating in my room," said Becky.

12
00:01:04.758 --> 00:01:09.155
"If I leave any crumbs, the rats and mice will eat them."

13
00:01:09.156 --> 00:01:12.908
"Rats and mice!" Sara was horrified.

14
00:01:12.909 --> 00:01:17.447
"There are always rats and mice in attics," said Becky.

15
00:01:17.448 --> 00:01:19.410
"But you get used to them, miss.

16
00:01:19.411 --> 00:01:23.083
I don't mind them as long as they don't run over my pillow!"

17
00:01:23.084 --> 00:01:29.335
Sara shuddered. "I don't think I could get used to them," she said.

18
00:01:29.336 --> 00:01:34.508
Whenever Sara went out, she searched for special treats for Becky.

19
00:01:34.509 --> 00:01:38.918
One day she brought back some meat pies.

20
00:01:38.919 --> 00:01:44.535
Becky's eyes sparkled when she saw them. "Oh, miss!" she said.

21
00:01:44.536 --> 00:01:46.646
"Those meat pies will fill me up.

22
00:01:46.647 --> 00:01:50.159
I mean, cake is nice, but it's not filling."

23
00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:56.665
So Sara brought Becky more meat pies, beef sandwiches, and sausages.

24
00:01:56.666 --> 00:02:01.596
Becky began to gain weight. She grew stronger too.

25
00:02:01.597 --> 00:02:05.256
Sara had no idea how much she meant to Becky.

26
00:02:05.257 --> 00:02:07.961
And it wasn't just because of the food.

27
00:02:07.962 --> 00:02:13.306
Sara always had a kind word for Becky and made her laugh every day.

28
00:02:13.307 --> 00:02:19.353
Becky's life had always been hard, and she had only rarely laughed or known joy.

29
00:02:19.354 --> 00:02:24.663
Now laughing with Sara made her feel as full as those meat pies did.

30
00:02:24.664 --> 00:02:30.132
She had something nice to think about every night when she went to bed.

31
00:02:30.133 --> 00:02:35.100
A few weeks before her eleventh birthday, Sara received a letter.

32
00:02:35.101 --> 00:02:39.369
It was from her father, who didn't seem as cheerful as usual.

33
00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:43.857
He said that he was sick and also worried about the diamond mines.

34
00:02:43.858 --> 00:02:48.358
But he'd still managed to make wonderful preparations for her birthday.

35
00:02:48.359 --> 00:02:51.887
He had ordered her an expensive gift from Paris.

36
00:02:51.888 --> 00:02:55.984
It was another doll with beautiful, handmade clothes.

37
00:02:55.985 --> 00:03:00.778
Then he'd wanted to know if a doll was still an acceptable gift for his daughter.

38
00:03:00.779 --> 00:03:05.007
I'm getting very old, Sara wrote back.

39
00:03:05.008 --> 00:03:08.102
This will probably be my last doll, Papa.

40
00:03:08.103 --> 00:03:14.212
No doll can ever take Emily's place, but I will respect the Last Doll very much.

41
00:03:14.213 --> 00:03:18.343
And I am sure that the school will love her too.

42
00:03:18.344 --> 00:03:23.172
In his bungalow in India, Captain Crewe burned with fever.

43
00:03:23.173 --> 00:03:29.409
When he received Sara's letter, he laughed as he had not for weeks.

44
00:03:29.410 --> 00:03:34.755
"How I'd love to have her arms around my neck right now!"

45
00:03:34.756 --> 00:03:39.031
When Sara's birthday arrived, the whole school was excited.

46
00:03:39.032 --> 00:03:43.439
After the morning lessons, the desks were all pushed aside.

47
00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:47.331
The plan was for Sara to open her presents in the schoolroom.

48
00:03:47.332 --> 00:03:51.546
Then everyone would go to Miss Minchin's sitting room for lunch.

49
00:03:51.547 --> 00:03:55.866
Sara returned to her sitting room for a few minutes before the party.

50
00:03:55.867 --> 00:04:01.097
There, on a table, she found a small package wrapped in brown paper.

51
00:04:01.098 --> 00:04:06.130
She opened it and found a square pincushion made of old red flannel.

52
00:04:06.131 --> 00:04:10.424
The pins had been arranged to spell "Happy Birthday."

53
00:04:10.425 --> 00:04:14.347
"I bet Becky made this!" cried Sara.

54
00:04:14.348 --> 00:04:16.668
Sara turned over her present.

55
00:04:16.669 --> 00:04:22.677
Pinned to the bottom of the pincushion was a card addressed to Miss Amelia Minchin.

56
00:04:22.678 --> 00:04:26.462
"Miss Amelia?" Sara was puzzled.

57
00:04:26.463 --> 00:04:31.072
Just then the door opened and Becky peeked into the room.

58
00:04:31.073 --> 00:04:33.917
She had a sweet grin on her face.

59
00:04:33.918 --> 00:04:37.098
"Do you like it, Miss Sara?"

60
00:04:37.099 --> 00:04:44.615
"Like it?" Sara cried. "Of course I do! You made this all by yourself!"

61
00:04:44.616 --> 00:04:48.627
Becky nodded happily, and her eyes looked damp.

62
00:04:48.628 --> 00:04:52.545
"The flannel isn't new, but I wanted to give you something.

63
00:04:52.546 --> 00:04:55.164
I knew you could pretend the flannel was satin.

64
00:04:55.165 --> 00:04:59.121
I tried to pretend the heads of the pins were diamonds."

65
00:04:59.122 --> 00:05:04.249
"It's wonderful, Becky. But I'm puzzled by the card."

66
00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:08.679
"Miss Amelia had thrown it away," Becky explained.

67
00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:11.612
"I hope it wasn't wrong to pick it out of the trash.

68
00:05:11.613 --> 00:05:15.272
It wouldn't be a proper present without a card."

69
00:05:15.273 --> 00:05:21.328
Sara ran to Becky and hugged her. "Oh, Becky!" she cried.

70
00:05:21.329 --> 00:05:24.715
"I love you! I really do."

71
00:05:24.716 --> 00:05:29.511
"Oh, miss," said Becky. "Thank you kindly."

72
00:05:29.512 --> 00:05:38.385
Sara didn't know why, but a large lump had filled her throat.
